\name{cellucid_camera_path_get}
\alias{cellucid_camera_path_get}
\title{Read the camera path}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_path_get(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{keyframes}, \code{playback}, \code{playing}, \code{return_to_start} (Ends with a return to the first keyframe), \code{seconds} (The whole path's length in seconds, holds included). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The camera path: each keyframe (label, camera, when it is reached, how long the camera rests there, the time of the transition after it), how it plays, its length, and whether it is playing.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera-path.get} (Camera path). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_camera_path_get(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
